# Ignore file for Dockerfile. Docker prefers an ignore file named after its
# Dockerfile and sitting beside it over a .dockerignore at the context root.
#
# Patterns stay relative to the context root, which is the repository root
# because the image needs both compat-tests/ and the packed nupkg under
# artifacts/. Everything else is excluded so the context stays small (step-down
# allow-list: a child can only be re-included if none of its parent directories
# are excluded).
*
!compat-tests
!artifacts
artifacts/*
!artifacts/BlackFox.MasterOfFoo
artifacts/BlackFox.MasterOfFoo/*
!artifacts/BlackFox.MasterOfFoo/Release
artifacts/BlackFox.MasterOfFoo/Release/*
!artifacts/BlackFox.MasterOfFoo/Release/*.nupkg
